{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 116, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing an existing conv on the last edge gives little extra capacity compared with replacing none, skip or pooling."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 5 is absent, edge 4 is the only learnable path into the output, so a conv there matters much more."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 5 when edge 4 is already none cuts off every conv path to the output."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 4 when edge 5 is none leaves the output fed only by edge 3, which badly degrades the cell."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Without a direct input-to-output skip, a skip on edge 0 provides a useful identity path instead of displacing a conv."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Without the edge-3 residual, a skip from the input to node 2 restores gradient flow, so it hurts less or helps."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "A skip into the output node partly substitutes for the missing edge-3 residual."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Without the edge-3 shortcut, an identity path into the output is valuable rather than a loss of conv capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling the empty direct input-to-output edge adds a short path, a bigger gain than replacin